# Fricke involution sends Ogg's unit to ℓ¹²u_ℓ⁻¹

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.coe_frickeInvolutionFull_modularUnitSeries`
(`79408102-26d3-5260-b18d-9dc1e6671f44`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `870e3474-6437-5122-8229-fc8052e94490`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $\ell$ be a prime. Inside the field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ of rational Laurent series,
[`ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L127) $\ell$ denotes the series
$u_\ell = \Delta \cdot (\Delta^{(\ell)})^{-1}$, where $\Delta$ is the Laurent series $q\prod_{n\ge
1}(1-q^n)^{24}$ built from the single term $q$ and the power series `dedekindEtaUnitQ`, and
$\Delta^{(\ell)}$ is its image under the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ given by `qExpand ℚ ℓ`.
Let `modularFunctionFieldFull ℓ` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$
generated by the set of series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $\ell$, and let
`hmem` be a witness that $u_\ell$ lies in that field. Let `frickeInvolutionFull ℓ` be the
$\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of this field chosen, if one exists, to satisfy `IsFrickeAutFull
ℓ`, i.e. to interchange `qExpand ℚ a jq` and `qExpand ℚ b jq` whenever $ab=\ell$ (and the identity
automorphism otherwise). The assertion is that the image of the element $u_\ell$ of
`modularFunctionFieldFull ℓ` under this automorphism, regarded again as a Laurent series, is
$\ell^{12}$ times $u_\ell^{-1}$, the scalar acting coefficientwise.

This is the classical behaviour of Ogg's modular unit $u_\ell = \Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{\ell})$ under
the Fricke involution $w_\ell$ on the modular function field of level $\ell$, namely $w_\ell(u_\ell)
= \ell^{12} u_\ell^{-1}$, recorded here at the level of $q$-expansions. It feeds the construction of
models and of residue/specialisation data for the curves $X_0(\ell)$ used further on.

